1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,467
Millions of people own stocks.

2
00:00:02,517 --> 00:00:05,715
On Robinhood Chain, they
can hold them as tokens.

3
00:00:05,765 --> 00:00:09,136
But a token earns nothing
while it sits in a wallet.

4
00:00:09,186 --> 00:00:13,131
On Wall Street, holders sell
covered calls for weekly income.

5
00:00:13,181 --> 00:00:15,686
But someone has to pick
the strike each week,

6
00:00:15,736 --> 00:00:17,288
and you have to trust them.

7
00:00:17,338 --> 00:00:19,165
On-chain it is harder:

8
00:00:19,215 --> 00:00:22,179
a multiplier that is easy to apply twice,

9
00:00:22,229 --> 00:00:24,119
prices that freeze on weekends,

10
00:00:24,169 --> 00:00:26,944
pause switches, and mid-week splits.

11
00:00:26,994 --> 00:00:28,811
So the tokens sit idle,

12
00:00:28,861 --> 00:00:31,536
or go to a manager nobody can check.

13
00:00:31,586 --> 00:00:35,371
Now imagine an AI agent that
picks the strike every week,

14
00:00:35,421 --> 00:00:38,173
and a contract that won't
let it break the rules.

15
00:00:38,223 --> 00:00:39,395
This is Strike:

16
00:00:39,445 --> 00:00:43,288
weekly options vaults for
Robinhood Chain stock tokens.

17
00:00:43,338 --> 00:00:46,725
Depositors earn a weekly premium in USDG.

18
00:00:46,775 --> 00:00:51,581
An AI agent picks the strike, inside
a mandate the contract enforces.

19
00:00:51,631 --> 00:00:55,040
Break the mandate, and its
bond goes to the depositors.

20
00:00:55,090 --> 00:00:58,968
The math runs on-chain, in
Rust on Arbitrum Stylus.

21
00:00:59,018 --> 00:01:03,837
And it is live on Robinhood Chain
testnet and Arbitrum Sepolia.

22
00:01:03,887 --> 00:01:06,432
Here is one week, inside Strike.

23
00:01:06,482 --> 00:01:10,381
Depositors put stock tokens in
a vault with a fixed mandate.

24
00:01:10,431 --> 00:01:13,329
An agent reads the
vault through MCP tools,

25
00:01:13,379 --> 00:01:15,280
and dry-runs its proposal.

26
00:01:15,330 --> 00:01:16,816
Then it proposes a call:

27
00:01:16,866 --> 00:01:20,296
a delta, an expiry, a size and a price.

28
00:01:20,346 --> 00:01:23,155
The Epoch Manager checks
it against the mandate,

29
00:01:23,205 --> 00:01:25,845
at prices from a guarded stock oracle.

30
00:01:25,895 --> 00:01:28,688
A Rust pricer on Stylus solves the strike,

31
00:01:28,738 --> 00:01:31,341
and a risk engine stress-tests it.

32
00:01:31,391 --> 00:01:35,045
If it passes, buyers pay premium in USDG.

33
00:01:35,095 --> 00:01:39,656
If not, it is rejected, and the
bond is slashed to depositors.

34
00:01:39,706 --> 00:01:42,349
Each decision is hashed
into a DecisionLog,

35
00:01:42,399 --> 00:01:46,219
and the agent has an ERC-8004 identity.

36
00:01:46,269 --> 00:01:48,736
After Friday's close the options settle,

37
00:01:48,786 --> 00:01:52,014
and the premium, less a
fee, goes to depositors.

38
00:01:52,064 --> 00:01:57,310
The same contracts run on Robinhood
Chain testnet and Arbitrum Sepolia.

39
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:58,629
Now one depositor:

40
00:01:58,679 --> 00:02:03,222
say Maya holds Tesla tokens, and
opens the covered-call vault.

41
00:02:03,272 --> 00:02:09,766
This week it sold the $369.86
call, all four options,

42
00:02:09,816 --> 00:02:12,846
to a buyer agent, for 10.01 USDG.

43
00:02:12,896 --> 00:02:17,054
At or below the strike, depositors
like Maya keep all of it.

44
00:02:17,104 --> 00:02:21,897
The buyer only profits above $372.36.

45
00:02:21,947 --> 00:02:23,817
She doesn't have to trust the agent:

46
00:02:23,867 --> 00:02:25,834
the limits are in the contract.

47
00:02:25,884 --> 00:02:29,530
Delta between 0.10 and 0.35.

48
00:02:29,580 --> 00:02:32,522
At least 95% of fair value.

49
00:02:32,572 --> 00:02:35,661
A yield of at least 0.05%.

50
00:02:35,711 --> 00:02:37,511
At most 80% sold,

51
00:02:37,562 --> 00:02:39,965
and 1 to 8 days to expiry.

52
00:02:40,015 --> 00:02:42,109
Nobody can change them.

53
00:02:42,159 --> 00:02:43,933
She can test the rules herself:

54
00:02:43,983 --> 00:02:47,926
the playground asks the deployed
Epoch Manager, with no wallet.

55
00:02:47,976 --> 00:02:51,491
An honest 0.20-delta call: accepted.

56
00:02:51,541 --> 00:02:53,608
A reckless at-the-money strike:

57
00:02:53,658 --> 00:02:55,931
rejected, delta out of band.

58
00:02:55,981 --> 00:02:59,984
A real one would cost the
agent 10 USDG of its bond,

59
00:03:00,034 --> 00:03:02,432
paid to depositors like Maya.

60
00:03:02,482 --> 00:03:04,901
Buyers pay a price set when they buy:

61
00:03:04,951 --> 00:03:08,917
the oracle spot moved 0.5% against them,

62
00:03:08,967 --> 00:03:13,112
priced with Black-Scholes, times
the agent's premium factor.

63
00:03:13,162 --> 00:03:15,256
Never below intrinsic value,

64
00:03:15,306 --> 00:03:18,952
so Monday's price can't be
picked off on Wednesday.

65
00:03:19,002 --> 00:03:22,336
Maya's vault ran for real on September 29.

66
00:03:22,386 --> 00:03:26,517
The seller agent asked for
a 0.20-delta Tesla call,

67
00:03:26,568 --> 00:03:33,005
and the contract solved the strike
on-chain: $369.86, accepted.

68
00:03:33,055 --> 00:03:36,108
Then a reckless agent
forced an at-the-money put.

69
00:03:36,158 --> 00:03:39,009
Rejected, and 10 USDG slashed:

70
00:03:39,060 --> 00:03:41,671
its bond went from 60 to 50.

71
00:03:41,721 --> 00:03:46,599
On the explorer it says Success:
a rejection is not a revert,

72
00:03:46,649 --> 00:03:50,121
and 10 USDG left the agent's bond.

73
00:03:50,721 --> 00:03:54,663
On Arbitrum Sepolia, Claude
planned the proposal itself.

74
00:03:54,713 --> 00:03:57,602
Through Claude Code and
Strike's MCP server,

75
00:03:57,652 --> 00:03:58,817
it read the vault,

76
00:03:58,867 --> 00:04:01,823
and dry-ran five
candidates with risk_check.

77
00:04:01,873 --> 00:04:06,783
It chose a 0.20 delta
at 105% of fair value,

78
00:04:06,833 --> 00:04:07,993
and wrote down why:

79
00:04:08,043 --> 00:04:11,991
mid-band, so a small move can't
push it out of the mandate.

80
00:04:12,041 --> 00:04:18,025
The contract solved the strike,
$364.29, and accepted it.

81
00:04:18,075 --> 00:04:19,076
On Arbiscan:

82
00:04:19,126 --> 00:04:23,158
a successful call to the Epoch
Manager, from the agent's signer.

83
00:04:23,208 --> 00:04:28,012
In the same run, a reckless put
was rejected with a 10 USDG slash,

84
00:04:28,062 --> 00:04:30,619
and a buyer took all 4 calls.

85
00:04:30,669 --> 00:04:33,363
Here is that covered call, in 3D.

86
00:04:33,413 --> 00:04:35,523
Across, Tesla's price.

87
00:04:35,573 --> 00:04:38,061
Front to back, days to expiry.

88
00:04:38,112 --> 00:04:40,491
Up, one covered share's value.

89
00:04:40,541 --> 00:04:45,755
At expiry, it bends flat
at the $364.29 strike:

90
00:04:45,805 --> 00:04:48,558
above it, the upside goes to the buyer.

91
00:04:48,608 --> 00:04:51,198
Below it, the depositor keeps the stock,

92
00:04:51,248 --> 00:04:54,942
plus $2.23 of premium per option.

93
00:04:54,992 --> 00:04:59,051
The math is written in Rust,
and runs on Arbitrum Stylus.

94
00:04:59,101 --> 00:05:02,891
Solving the strike takes 48
Black-Scholes evaluations.

95
00:05:02,941 --> 00:05:08,064
In Stylus, that costs 6.5 times
less gas than in Solidity,

96
00:05:08,114 --> 00:05:11,366
and the whole proposal 3.3 times less.

97
00:05:11,416 --> 00:05:13,611
Every run leaves a decision record:

98
00:05:13,661 --> 00:05:18,537
what the agent saw, what it chose
and why, and what the contract said.

99
00:05:18,587 --> 00:05:21,838
Its hash is anchored in
the DecisionLog contract.

100
00:05:21,888 --> 00:05:26,030
Hash the published file again,
and it matches the chain.

101
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:30,888
On the leaderboard, the agent's
public ERC-8004 identity:

102
00:05:30,938 --> 00:05:36,475
114 on Robinhood Chain testnet,
253 on Arbitrum Sepolia.

103
00:05:36,525 --> 00:05:42,667
Any agent can join the same way, through
the public MCP server, with no allow-list.

104
00:05:42,717 --> 00:05:45,072
This monitor reads every stock token

105
00:05:45,122 --> 00:05:47,502
on Robinhood Chain mainnet, live.

106
00:05:47,552 --> 00:05:53,329
Nvidia's multiplier, 1.000775,
is already in the price,

107
00:05:53,379 --> 00:05:56,030
so Strike never applies it twice.

108
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:59,843
Over 403 weekly epochs since 2019,

109
00:05:59,893 --> 00:06:04,193
the covered call cut
volatility by 25 to 46%.

110
00:06:04,243 --> 00:06:06,524
But it lagged holding on every ticker:

111
00:06:06,574 --> 00:06:13,198
Tesla returned 23.1% a year in
the vault, against 44.0% held.

112
00:06:13,248 --> 00:06:16,734
And it assumes buyers take
the full size every week,

113
00:06:16,784 --> 00:06:19,422
which no contract can guarantee.

114
00:06:19,472 --> 00:06:22,849
The proof page puts every
claim next to its evidence.

115
00:06:22,899 --> 00:06:24,988
891 tests and proofs,

116
00:06:25,038 --> 00:06:27,745
99.3% line coverage,

117
00:06:27,795 --> 00:06:30,177
nine properties proven with Halmos,

118
00:06:30,227 --> 00:06:33,766
and all 11 internal-review findings fixed.

119
00:06:33,816 --> 00:06:35,177
Who else is here?

120
00:06:35,227 --> 00:06:39,417
Stonkhouse and Archer Markets, on
Robinhood Chain, are order books:

121
00:06:39,467 --> 00:06:42,700
traders and writers pick the
strike and set the price.

122
00:06:42,750 --> 00:06:45,972
Ribbon, Derive and
Thetanuts, on other chains,

123
00:06:46,022 --> 00:06:50,009
sell options on crypto by
auction, order book or RFQ.

124
00:06:50,059 --> 00:06:55,513
Tilt Protocol, a past winner, has
an AI manage tokenized-asset vaults.

125
00:06:55,563 --> 00:07:01,332
It sells no options, and its sources don't
describe what limits that AI on-chain.

126
00:07:01,382 --> 00:07:06,879
In Strike, a bonded agent proposes, the
contract checks an immutable mandate,

127
00:07:06,929 --> 00:07:09,470
prices every buy at the oracle,

128
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:12,620
and makes a rule-breaking
agent pay the depositors.

129
00:07:12,670 --> 00:07:15,788
The stock-token traps are
handled in the contract.

130
00:07:15,838 --> 00:07:19,193
For a holder: income without
handing over the keys,

131
00:07:19,243 --> 00:07:22,247
and every decision checkable on-chain.

132
00:07:22,297 --> 00:07:26,378
Weekend freezes: settle on
the first price after expiry.

133
00:07:26,428 --> 00:07:30,242
The multiplier: never applied,
tested on a mainnet fork.

134
00:07:30,292 --> 00:07:34,618
Trusting an agent: a fixed
mandate, a bond, and slashing.

135
00:07:34,668 --> 00:07:39,485
On-chain pricing: Rust on
Stylus, 6.5 times cheaper.

136
00:07:39,535 --> 00:07:43,927
What's not done: there is no
external audit, it is testnet only,

137
00:07:43,977 --> 00:07:47,586
and both epochs settle
on Friday 2 October.

138
00:07:47,636 --> 00:07:50,871
Strike: options on Robinhood
Chain and Arbitrum,

139
00:07:50,921 --> 00:07:53,978
run by agents the contract
holds to a mandate.

140
00:07:54,028 --> 00:07:58,495
Try the playground at
strike-options.vercel.app.

141
00:07:58,545 --> 00:08:01,436
It is unaudited, and on testnet.
